astral bodies here. That's for the High Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Astral; <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">of, connected with, or resembling the stars. For example Astral Navigation aka navigation by the stars.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T14:24:48-07:00","id":1446332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444504-so-assuming-rage-across-the-heavens-is-still-canon?p=1446307#post1446307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Astral; <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">of, connected with, or resembling the stars. For example Astral Navigation aka navigation by the stars.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to use plain language for a jargon-heavy setting discussion regarding the spirit worlds of the WoD is not a good swerve. Especially not when there's a region of the Umbra named the same thing as the word you decided to use. A better choice would have been astronomical body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T18:20:55-07:00","id":1447067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444504-so-assuming-rage-across-the-heavens-is-still-canon?p=1446332#post1446332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Trying to use plain language for a jargon-heavy setting discussion regarding the spirit worlds of the WoD is not a good swerve. Especially not when there's a region of the Umbra named the same thing as the word you decided to use. A better choice would have been astronomical body.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except they aren't astronomical bodies. That would be the material world versions which may or may not exist depending on Mage. Celestial bodies might work as there is a Celestial Court for each.. I think though only the Incarna will show up for the players.<br /> <br /> You must be this tall to be a Celestine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T13:56:59-07:00","id":1447262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444504-so-assuming-rage-across-the-heavens-is-still-canon?p=1447067#post1447067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except they aren't astronomical bodies. That would be the material world versions which may or may not exist depending on Mage. Celestial bodies might work as there is a Celestial Court for each.. I think though only the Incarna will show up for the players.<br /> <br /> You must be this tall to be a Celestine.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are astronomical bodies and a number of other things besides. Celestial bodies and courts, though, is cruising for confusion, as celestines are in a deeper layer of the spirit world than the Planetary Incarnae in the Aetherial Realm. Celestines are also noted as being very independent from and enabling material existence - though we're also given some information that can get difficult to splice together, like how using the moon as a shield against an asteroid launched by Rorg causes Luna enough pain and injury to reduce her to Incarna status (at least according to Apocalypse), but that if the moon were destroyed, Luna could recreate it. Presumably, there was also something more that the massive Wyrm-spirit that scattered Rorg's former planetary body did to knock him down to just one planetary Incarna without the potential to heal back (or they might not be going with that story threat anymore; some of the information in RatH seems to be differently worded in W20 materials, possibly based on a changing understanding of astronomical bodies and their origins).<br /> <br /> Again, if you want a story where human belief drastically changes spirits, that's much more Mage's speed, especially where the Astral Umbra is concerned. The Middle Umbra is probably more concerned with long-standing orbital paths. In Werewolf, Meros can be a Planetary Incarna on par with the others, with a Patron Celestine who is similarly of spiritual stature just because, and that's where we can largely leave things in terms of backstory and metaphysical explanations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T21:42:31-07:00","id":1447337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444504-so-assuming-rage-across-the-heavens-is-still-canon?p=1447262#post1447262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Again, if you want a story where human belief drastically changes spirits, that's much more Mage's speed, especially where the Astral Umbra is concerned. The Middle Umbra is probably more concerned with long-standing orbital paths. In Werewolf, Meros can be a Planetary Incarna on par with the others, with a Patron Celestine who is similarly of spiritual stature just because, and that's where we can largely leave things in terms of backstory and metaphysical explanations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not a big fan of Pluto as realm for the various reasons Pluto was downgraded from planet IRL. There is nothing about it special that makes it a &quot;proper&quot; planet. Giving Meros a court that includes the Oort cloud or multiple bodies would make sense given Rorg exists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}